# TwinCAT MCP Fast Syntax & Semantic Checker

Use when the user asks to check syntax, validate code without opening Visual Studio / XAE, run a quick lint, or `/twincat3-cmd-check-syntax`. Detailed workflow: skill `twincat3-check-syntax`.

## Tools (file-based, no COM/XAE session required)

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `twincat_check_syntax` | Fast ST syntax, AST parsing, and semantic validation (TC-DECL-*, TC-STMT-*, TC-EXPR-*, TC-SEM-*) |

No `twincat_open` needed. Operates directly on `.TcPOU`, `.TcDUT`, `.TcGVL`, `.TcIO`, `.plcproj`, or `.sln` files via `twincat_core` in milliseconds.

## Core parameters (`twincat_check_syntax`)

| Parameter | Default | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|---------|
| `path` | `""` | File, folder, `.plcproj`, or `.sln`. If empty, auto-detects project. |
| `recursive` | `true` | Recurse into subfolders when path is a directory |
| `include_warnings` | `true` | Include severity=WARNING diagnostics (e.g. TC-SEM-007 narrowing warnings) |

## Checked Diagnostic Categories

1. **Declaration Rules (`TC-DECL-001..007`)**:
   - `TC-DECL-001`: `FUNCTION`s must declare an explicit return type
   - `TC-DECL-002`: `PROPERTY`s must declare an explicit data type
   - `TC-DECL-003`: `CONSTANT` variables must have an initial value
   - `TC-DECL-004`: `VAR_IN_OUT` cannot have an initial value
   - `TC-DECL-005`: `VAR_TEMP` cannot be `RETAIN` or `PERSISTENT`
   - `TC-DECL-006`: `INTERFACE` declarations cannot contain `VAR` blocks
   - `TC-DECL-007`: Array lower bound cannot exceed upper bound (`ARRAY[10..5]`)

2. **Statement & Expression Rules (`TC-STMT-*`, `TC-EXPR-*`)**:
   - `TC-STMT-001`: `EXIT` is only valid inside a loop (`FOR`, `WHILE`, `REPEAT`)
   - `TC-STMT-002`: `CONTINUE` is only valid inside a loop
   - `TC-STMT-004`: Undefined `JMP` target label
   - `TC-EXPR-002`: Invalid assignment target (assigning to literal or non-lvalue)

3. **Semantic Rules (`TC-SEM-001..007`)**:
   - `TC-SEM-001`: Unknown data type in variable / struct field
   - `TC-SEM-002`: Duplicate identifier in same scope
   - `TC-SEM-003`: `FUNCTION_BLOCK` fails to implement all interface methods/properties
   - `TC-SEM-004`: Cyclic inheritance detected (`EXTENDS`)
   - `TC-SEM-005`: Cannot instantiate `ABSTRACT FUNCTION_BLOCK`
   - `TC-SEM-006`: Incompatible type assignment or non-BOOL condition (ERROR)
   - `TC-SEM-007`: Implicit narrowing, precision loss, or sign change (WARNING)

## Typical usage

**Single file check:**
```
twincat_check_syntax(path="POUs/FB_Motor.TcPOU")
```

**Project / Folder check:**
```
twincat_check_syntax(path="solution/twincat3-solution")
```

**Errors only (suppress warnings):**
```
twincat_check_syntax(include_warnings=false)
```
